\n\\[ y = 9 \\]\n\nNow, substitute \\(y = 9\\) back into \\(x = 3y\\):\n\\[ x = 3 \\cdot 9 = 27 \\]\n\nTherefore, \\(x + y = 27 + 9 = 36\\).\n\nThe most reliable candidate answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{36}\n\\]", "cimr_extracted_answer": "36"}}
