:\n\n\\[\n\\tan \\theta = \\left| \\frac{m_1 - m_2}{1 + m_1 m_2} \\right|\n\\]\n\nHere, \\(m_1 = 2\\) and \\(m_2 = \\frac{1}{3}\\). Plugging these values into the formula, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\tan \\theta = \\left| \\frac{2 - \\frac{1}{3}}{1 + 2 \\cdot \\frac{1}{3}} \\right| = \\left| \\frac{\\frac{6}{3} - \\frac{1}{3}}{1 + \\frac{2}{3}} \\right| = \\left| \\frac{\\frac{5}{3}}{\\frac{5}{3}} \\right| = 1\n\\]\n\nSince \\(\\tan \\theta = 1\\), the angle \\(\\theta\\) is \\(45^\\circ\\). Therefore, the degree measure of the acute angle formed by the lines is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{45}\n\\]", "cimr_extracted_answer": "45"}}
