eries.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{3159}\\).", "cimr_extracted_answer": "3159"}, "cimr_answer_only": {"selected_idx": -1, "predicted_answer": "3159", "is_correct": true, "raw_score": NaN, "norm_score": NaN, "cluster_size": -1, "alpha": NaN, "tau": 0.85, "method": "cimr_answer_only", "fmax": 0.625, "H": 0.9544340029220797, "He": 0.3181446676406932, "M": 2, "r": 0.25, "n_clusters": 2, "judge_tokens": 573, "judge_elapsed_sec": 0.0, "fallback": false, "clusters_shown": [{"cluster_id": 0, "size": 3, "max_prm": 0.9961, "mean_prm": 0.9883, "agreement": 1.0, "modal_answer": "3159", "n_variants": 1}, {"cluster_id": 1, "size": 5, "max_prm": 0.9922, "mean_prm": 0.767, "agreement": 0.8, "modal_answer": "3159", "n_variants": 2}], "judge_raw_response": "To solve the problem \\(2^3 - 1^3 + 4^3 - 3^3 + 6^3 - 5^3 + \\dots + 18^3 - 17^3\\), we start by examining the pattern in the sequence. Each pair of terms can be simplified as follows:\n\n\\[\n(2n)^3 - (2n-1)^3\n\\]\n\nWe can expand and simplify this expression:\n\n\\[\n(2n)^3 - (2n-1)^3 = 8n^3 - (8n^3 - 12n^2 + 6n - 1) = 12n^2 - 6n + 1\n\\]\n\nSo, the original sum can be rewritten as:\n\n\\[\n\\sum_{n=1}^{9} (12n^2 - 6n + 1)\n\\]\n\nWe can break this sum into three separate sums:\n\n\\[\n12 \\sum_{n=1}^{9} n^2 - 6 \\sum_{n=1}^{9} n + \\sum_{n=1}^{9} 1\n\\]\n\nWe know the formulas for the sum of the first \\(n\\) squares and the sum of the first \\(n\\) natural numbers:\n\n\\[\n\\sum_{n=1}^{9} n^2 = \\frac{9 \\cdot 10 \\cdot 19}{6} = 285\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sum_{n=1}^{9} n = \\frac{9 \\cdot 10}{2} = 45\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sum_{n=1}^{9} 1 = 9\n\\]\n\nSubstituting these values into our expression, we get:\n\n\\[\n12 \\cdot 285 - 6 \\cdot 45 + 9 = 3420 - 270 + 9 = 3159\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of the given expression is \\(\\boxed{3159}\\).", "cimr_extracted_answer": "3159"}}
