nator. The least common multiple of 3, 4, and 8 is 24. Multiply every term by 24:\n\n\\[\n24 \\left( \\frac{1}{3}P \\right) + 24 \\left( \\frac{7}{4} \\right) = 24 \\left( \\frac{3}{4}P \\right) + 24 \\left( \\frac{1}{8} \\right)\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n8P + 42 = 18P + 3\n\\]\n\nNow, isolate \\( P \\) by subtracting \\( 8P \\) and 3 from both sides of the equation:\n\n\\[\n42 - 3 = 18P - 8P\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n39 = 10P\n\\]\n\nSolve for \\( P \\) by dividing both sides by 10:\n\n\\[\nP = \\frac{39}{10}\n\\]\n\nThe weight of a large pizza is \\( \\frac{39}{10} \\) pounds. The problem asks for \\( m - n \\) where the weight is expressed in the form \\( \\frac{m}{n} \\) with \\( m \\) and \\( n \\) relatively prime. Here, \\( m = 39 \\) and \\( n = 10 \\), so:\n\n\\[\nm - n = 39 - 10 = 29\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{29}\n\\]", "cimr_extracted_answer": "29"}}
