6176 \\equiv 6 \\pmod{10}\\).\n8. If \\(n+1 \\equiv 7 \\pmod{10}\\), then \\((n+1)^{10} \\equiv 7^{10} \\equiv 282475249 \\equiv 9 \\pmod{10}\\).\n9. If \\(n+1 \\equiv 8 \\pmod{10}\\), then \\((n+1)^{10} \\equiv 8^{10} \\equiv 1073741824 \\equiv 4 \\pmod{10}\\).\n10. If \\(n+1 \\equiv 9 \\pmod{10}\\), then \\((n+1)^{10} \\equiv 9^{10} \\equiv 3486784401 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{10}\\).\n11. If \\(n+1 \\equiv 10 \\pmod{10}\\), then \\((n+1)^{10} \\equiv 10^{10} \\equiv 0 \\pmod{10}\\).\n\nFrom the above cases, we see that the possible remainders when \\((n+1)^{10}\\) is divided by 10 are 0, 1, 4, 5, 6, and 9. Since \\(n\\) is a positive integer less than or equal to 10, \\(n+1\\) can be any integer from 2 to 11. Therefore, the possible remainders are 0, 1, 4, 5, 6, and 9.\n\nGiven the candidate answers and their evidence, the most reliable candidate answer is \"5\" with a count of 5, a best_PRM of 0.8398, and a mean_PRM of 0.7320. This suggests that \"5\" is a common and consistent answer.\n\nThus, the remainder when \\(K\\) is divided by 10 is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{5}\n\\]", "cimr_extracted_answer": "5"}}
