are:\n\n\\[\nx_1 = 6 + 2\\sqrt{5} \\quad \\text{and} \\quad x_2 = 6 - 2\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\n\nThe positive difference between the \\(x\\)-coordinates of \\(A\\) and \\(B\\) is:\n\n\\[\n| x_1 - x_2 | = | (6 + 2\\sqrt{5}) - (6 - 2\\sqrt{5}) | = | 6 + 2\\sqrt{5} - 6 + 2\\sqrt{5} | = | 4\\sqrt{5} | = 4\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\n\nThe final answer is in the form \\(m\\sqrt{n}\\), where \\(m = 4\\) and \\(n = 5\\). Therefore, \\(m + n = 4 + 5 = 9\\).\n\nThe final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{9}\n\\]", "cimr_extracted_answer": "9"}}
