wers. The conditions are:\n\n1. \\(abcd = 2^6 \\cdot 3^9 \\cdot 5^7\\)\n2. \\(\\text{lcm}(a, b) = 2^3 \\cdot 3^2 \\cdot 5^3\\)\n3. \\(\\text{lcm}(a, c) = 2^3 \\cdot 3^3 \\cdot 5^3\\)\n4. \\(\\text{lcm}(a, d) = 2^3 \\cdot 3^3 \\cdot 5^3\\)\n5. \\(\\text{lcm}(b, c) = 2^1 \\cdot 3^3 \\cdot 5^2\\)\n6. \\(\\text{lcm}(b, d) = 2^2 \\cdot 3^3 \\cdot 5^2\\)\n7. \\(\\text{lcm}(c, d) = 2^2 \\cdot 3^3 \\cdot 5^2\\)\n\nFrom these conditions, we can deduce the prime factorizations of \\(a\\), \\(b\\), \\(c\\), and \\(d\\). Let:\n\\[a = 2^{x_1} \\cdot 3^{y_1} \\cdot 5^{z_1}\\]\n\\[b = 2^{x_2} \\cdot 3^{y_2} \\cdot 5^{z_2}\\]\n\\[c = 2^{x_3} \\cdot 3^{y_3} \\cdot 5^{z_3}\\]\n\\[d = 2^{x_4} \\cdot 3^{y_4} \\cdot 5^{z_4}\\]\n\nThe conditions on the least common multiples give us the following system of equations:\n1. \\(\\max(x_1, x_2) = 3\\)\n2. \\(\\max(x_1, x_3) = 3\\)\n3. \\(\\max(x_1, x_4) = 3\\)\n4. \\(\\max(x_2, x_3) = 1\\)\n5. \\(\\max(x_2, x_4) = 2\\)\n6. \\(\\max(x_3, x_4) = 2\\)\n\nFrom these equations, we can deduce that \\(x_1 = 3\\) and \\(x_2, x_3, x_4\\) must be such that \\(\\max(x_2, x_3) = 1\\) and \\(\\max(x_2, x_4) = 2\\) and \\(\\max(x_3, x_4) = 2\\). The only way to satisfy these conditions is if \\(x_2 = 1\\), \\(x_3 = 1\\), and \\(x_4 = 2\\).\n\nNext, we consider the powers of 3:\n1. \\(\\max(y_1, y_2) = 2\\)\n2. \\(\\max(y_1, y_3) = 3\\)\n3. \\(\\max(y_1, y_4) = 3\\)\n4. \\(\\max(y_2, y_3) = 3\\)\n5. \\(\\max(y_2, y_4) = 3\\)\n6. \\(\\max(y_3, y_4) = 3\\)\n\nFrom these equations, we can deduce that \\(y_1 = 2\\) and \\(y_2, y_3, y_4\\) must be such that \\(\\max(y_2, y_3) = 3\\) and \\(\\max(y_2, y_4) = 3\\) and \\(\\max(y_3, y_4) = 3\\). The only way to satisfy these conditions is if \\(y_2 = 3\\), \\(y_3 = 3\\), and \\(y_4 = 3\\).\n\nFinally, we consider the powers of 5:\n1. \\(\\max(z_1, z_2) = 3\\)\n2. \\(\\max(z_1, z_3) = 3\\)\n3. \\(\\max(z_1, z_4) = 3\\)\n4. \\(\\max(z_2, z_3) = 2\\)\n5. \\(\\max(z_2, z_4) = 2\\)\n6. \\(\\max(z_3, z_4) = 2\\)\n\nFrom these equations, we can deduce that \\(z_1 = 3\\) and \\(z_2, z_3, z_4\\) must be such that \\(\\max(z_2, z_3) = 2\\) and \\(\\max(z_2, z_4) = 2\\) and \\(\\max(z_3, z_4) = 2\\). The only way to satisfy these conditions is if \\(z_2 = 2\\), \\(z_3 = 2\\), and \\(z_4 = 2\\).\n\nTherefore, the prime factorizations of \\(a\\), \\(b\\), \\(c\\), and \\(d\\) are:\n\\[a = 2^3 \\cdot 3^2 \\cdot 5^3\\]\n\\[b = 2^1 \\cdot 3^3 \\cdot 5^2\\]\n\\[c = 2^1 \\cdot 3^3 \\cdot 5^2\\]\n\\[d = 2^2 \\cdot 3^3 \\cdot 5^2\\]\n\nThe greatest common divisor of \\(a\\), \\(b\\), \\(c\\), and \\(d\\) is:\n\\[\\text{gcd}(a, b, c, d) = 2^1 \\cdot 3^2 \\cdot 5^2 = 2 \\cdot 9 \\cdot 25 = 450\\]\n\nThus, the answer is:\n\\[\\boxed{450}\\]", "cimr_extracted_answer": "450"}}
