x) \\) is negative.\n   - For \\( x \\in (2, 3) \\), the factors \\( (x-1) \\) and \\( (x-2) \\) are positive and the factors \\( (x-3), (x-4), \\ldots, (x-10) \\) are negative. Since there are 8 negative factors and the number of negative factors is even, \\( P(x) \\) is positive.\n   - This pattern continues. For \\( x \\in (k, k+1) \\) where \\( k \\) is odd, \\( P(x) \\) is positive, and for \\( x \\in (k, k+1) \\) where \\( k \\) is even, \\( P(x) \\) is negative.\n\n3. **Count the number of positive intervals**: The intervals where \\( P(x) \\) is positive are \\( (-\\infty, 1) \\), \\( (2, 3) \\), \\( (4, 5) \\), \\( (6, 7) \\), \\( (8, 9) \\), and \\( (10, \\infty) \\). There are 6 such intervals.\n\nTherefore, the number of intervals on which \\( P(x) \\) is positive is \\(\\boxed{6}\\).", "cimr_extracted_answer": "6"}}
