efore, the fraction \\(\\frac{-(\\log n)^2 + 2 \\log n}{\\log n - 3}\\) is non-negative for \\( 1 \\leq n \\leq 100 \\).\n\nThus, the expression \\(\\sqrt{\\frac{\\log (n^2) - (\\log n)^2}{\\log n - 3}}\\) represents a real number for all integers \\( n \\) in the range \\( 1 \\leq n \\leq 100 \\). The number of integers in this range is:\n\\[\n100 - 1 + 1 = 100.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{100}.\n\\]", "cimr_extracted_answer": "100"}}
